From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: upstream 0056's restart frames behind a
 switch (default off); log every auto pacing decision

Upstream (edde746/mpv-build ff1e806, patch 0056): after a seek the third
and fourth frames went to the layers without their subtitles, and at a
resume the first frame reached the layers too late for the video layer but
not the OSD layer (Plezy's HDMI captures on a 3rd generation Apple TV 4K).
Ported onto 0307 behind --avfoundation-restart-frames (default no: every
path below is skipped and the VO and vo.c behave as before):

- for the first 8 timed frames after the start, a seek or a resume, a frame
  waits for its own subtitles at least 25 ms, behind or not, and as long as
  its deadline allows while the render thread is not behind, until one such
  wait runs out (avf_osd_restart_wait_until());
- such a frame whose refresh is then less than 3.5 refreshes past its
  hand-over is stamped whole refreshes later (avf_host_restart_stamp_ns()).
  0307 holds the hand-over for its pacing point, under a refresh after the
  stamp is made, so the hand-over is taken as a refresh from now; 0307's
  pacing stamp moves with it. The frames after follow it as any frame does
  (avf_host_present_ns()). With 0307's short lead (1.3 to 2.3 refreshes) the
  ninth frame then comes back to the ordinary schedule, so a frame or two
  share a refresh there; the switch is meant to be tried with a long queue
  lead as well as without;
- vo.c tells the driver of a pause or a resume under the lock that picks
  the frame, before drawing it, when the driver asks (vo->pause_with_frame,
  set from the switch); otherwise as before.

The upstream 0054 display link is not taken: 0307's refresh clock gives the
grid. Upstream's change to 0049's deferred OSD lists is not needed (0049 is
not in this series).

Logged (verbose level): the switch in the "switches" line and run tag
(r0/r1); "restart-frames after <start|seek|unpause>: N moved by R
refreshes, W waited (G gave up)" when a window ends; and every auto pacing
decision, "vsync-snap pace moved|held|settled: <from> -> <to>; window shown
N dropped D (S set aside), stay before; <s> after <start|seek|unpause>", so
a point moved on a misread after a seek is visible.

Host tests: test_avf_osd_ahead.sh (restart waits), test_avf_subref.sh
(restart stamp).

LOCAL TEST ONLY: not pushed, not run on a device.

